d ET loudly announced Spielberg  is perhaps the greatest commercial  filmmaker alive it was a cultural  phenomenon easily the highest grossing  film of its year and it holds up  spectacularly today  [Music]  on the other end of the sci-fi spectrum  is Starship Troopers Paul Verhoeven's  bold dark satirical 1997 film very  loosely based on the Robert Heinlein  novel of the same name it's an  action-packed blood-soaked hilarious  good time with ver joven operating at  the peak of his craft the film  underperformed at the box office and  divided critics but it's satirical edge  has made it a cult classic in the years  since its release  both films will hit Netflix on June 1st  June is shaping up to be a great month  for dramatic films over at Netflix over  the next four weeks the streamer plans  to roll out everything from Academy  Award nominees to independent foreign  films and everything in between starting  on June 1st you'll be able to stream the  help and the classic musical West Side  Story among others the help is a popular  2011 period film based on the Kathryn  Stockett novel of the same name while  West Side Story is the definitive  feature film adaptation of the iconic  American Musical fortunately the eye  candy doesn't end there Netflix plans to  keep doling out the drama in a steady  flow throughout the month June 3rd will  see the release of Lady Bird a 2017 Best  Picture nominee from director Greta  Gerwig then on June 10th we get access  to middlemen a 2009 film about a man who  gets mixed up with the Russian mob June  12th brings a brand-new Spike Lee joint  the five Bloods starring chadwick  boseman the film follows four soldiers  who returned to Vietnam after the war to  look for treasure on the surface the  five Bloods looks something like a cross  between three kings and Apocalypse Now  but with Spike Lee at the helm you know  you're in for something brand new and  unforgettable finally Netflix plans to  round out the month with the foreign  film adieu an anthology film of sorts  that tells three interconnected stories  each taking place on the border between  Morocco and Spain look for that on the  30th there's never a bad time for  laughter and Netflix has got you covered  next month with a wide array of highbrow  lowbrow middlebrow and just about every  brow comedy you can imagine right at the  top of the month Netflix is poised to  drop a set of outstanding comedy films  spanning decades the earliest offering  on the list is 1976's Bad News Bears a  classic underdog sports comedy about a  washed-up alcoholic minor league  baseball player who takes on the  Herculean task of coaching a losing  little league team to success we also  get 1995's coming-of-age clueless the  film that made valley girl culture a  national phenomenon it stars Alicia  Silverstone Paul Rudd and the late  Brittany Murphy in a teen comedy for the  ages  if it's a concussion you have to keep  her conscious okay ask for question what  seven-ton says stuff she knows if you're  in the mood for something on the sillier  side Netflix has several notable options  for you available right away on June 1st  observe and report is a hilarious Seth  Rogen vehicle about a schlubby mall cop  on a mission to catch a flasher  terrorizing his turf walk hard the Dewey  Cox story written by Jake Kasdan and  Judd Apatow stars john c reilly in an  irreverent satire of the iconic Johnny  Cash biopic walk the line the right kid  is gonna die tonight and what comedy  list would be complete without a little  Sandman action you don't mess with the  Zohan is a classic Adam Sandler flick  concerning an Israeli special operator  who's grown weary with his violent life  and dreams of retiring as a hairstylist  mid-month dreamer plans to freshen up  its offerings with the addition of baby  mama a 2008 comedy starring Tina Fey as  a career woman who engages the services  of a reluctant layabout played by Amy  Poehler to be your pregnancy surrogate  what is water  horrible look for that on the 16th and  on June 26th Netflix is releasing  Eurovision Song Contest  the story of fire saga which concerns  two icelandic musicians vying for fame  and glory at the annual Eurovision  contest Will Ferrell and Rachel McAdams  have given us a glimpse of their  characters in the form of a music video  promising the kind of goofball comedy  that only Will Ferrell could deliver  given the wide variety June really does  have something for every comedy fan  while we might not associate the early  days of summer with spine-tingling  thrillers fans of the genre will tell  you that every season is horror season  if you're not or do fear rather because  Netflix has your back the streamers June  editions include horror and thriller  films new and old everything from tense  psychological thrillers to supernatural  gore fests beginning on the 1st of the  month  subscribers will have access to the  whole spectrum of rights you can settle  in with a plate of fava beans and nice  ki  to watch Anthony Hopkins as Hannibal  Lecter in Silence of the Lambs if  watching the famous cannibal  psychologically tormentors Clarice  doesn't do it for you he can always  navigate over to watch David Fincher's  zodiac a dramatized take on the  historical hunt for the Zodiac killer  the most prolific unsolved serial killer  case in modern history still not finding  anything to your liking 1991's Cape Fear  also streaming on the 1st of June is an  underappreciated psychological thriller  from Academy award-winning director  Martin Scorsese starring Robert De Niro  in one of his most unhinged roles ever  later in the month Netflix subscribers  can expect a new injection of horror  content in the form of to Blum house  productions first to arrive is Greg  McLean's terrifying supernatural horror  film The Darkness on June 16th the  darkness stars Kevin Bacon and Radha  Mitchell as unfortunate vacationers who  stumble upon an ancient evil on their  family trip to the Grand Canyon  after that flick has you hooked on Blum  House's unique aesthetic you can tune  into Scott Stewart's dark skies on June  22nd this 2013 science fiction horror  film stars Keri Russell Josh Hamilton  and the incomparable JK Simmons as the  residents of an unnamed American city  gripped by mysterious phenomena for the  last few years Netflix has been giving a  platform to the boldest and brightest  stars of the comedy world the trend will  continue in June 2020 when three very  distinct stand-up specials from masters  of the craft drop on the streaming  platform if you're in need of a good  belly laugh you know where to turn On  June 12th  you can catch a Netflix first comedian  jo koy whom you'll recognize from his  previous Netflix stand-up specials or  his stint as a panelist on Chelsea  Lately filmed his latest special in the  Philippines jo koy in his elements isn't  just stand-up though the comedian  brought along a group of fellow Filipino  American entertainers who had never been  to the island nation before to celebrate  their culture with a lot of love and a  lot of laughs  specials by two bona fide  comedy legends are dropping later in the  month on June 23rd Eric Andre makes his  Netflix debut with a new special that  sees the comedian tackling issues as  diverse as the war on drugs - the  legitimacy of fart jokes you can follow  that up on June 30th with another  Netflix debut from a comedy veteran  George Lopez provides some of his  signature humorous and heartfelt  insights on politics race and Latino  culture in his latest special will do it  for half fans of Netflix original series  are going to have a bountiful start to  their summer in June the streaming  service is dropping new seasons of some  of its most well-loved shows as well as  plenty of other series to keep you up  late hitting play next episode in the  first half of the month we're getting  the final season of the family-friendly  reboot fuller house on the second and  the final ins